1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:17,628
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is May twenty-fifth. Today's story: Tokyo might run its trains twenty-four hours a day. Right now, trains stop around midnight. That could change. Let's listen.

2
00:00:18,228 --> 00:00:25,788
[News] 東京都は、電車を24時間走らせることを考えています。

3
00:00:26,487 --> 00:00:36,712
[News] 今、東京の電車は夜12時ごろに止まります。朝5時まで電車はありません。

4
00:00:37,411 --> 00:00:46,076
[News] 夜遅くまで働く人や、外国からの旅行者にとって、これは不便です。

5
00:00:46,776 --> 00:00:54,048
[News] まず、金曜日と土曜日の夜だけ、試してみる予定です。

6
00:00:54,747 --> 00:01:00,531
[News] 使う路線は、山手線と中央線です。

7
00:01:01,231 --> 00:01:09,823
[News] でも、夜の間に線路の点検をしているので、安全の問題があります。

8
00:01:10,524 --> 00:01:21,756
[News] 東京都の担当者は、「安全が一番大切です。よく調べてから決めます」と言いました。

9
00:01:22,456 --> 00:01:24,087
[Host] Let's break it down.

10
00:01:24,688 --> 00:01:26,463
[Host] The first sentence.

11
00:01:27,063 --> 00:01:35,176
[Slow] 東京都は、電車を24時間走らせることを考えています。

12
00:01:35,975 --> 00:01:43,463
[Host] The Tokyo Metropolitan Government is thinking about running trains twenty-four hours a day. Let's look at the key words.

13
00:01:44,063 --> 00:01:46,296
[Vocab] 電車

14
00:01:46,695 --> 00:01:52,959
[Host] Train. One of the first words you learn in Japanese. You'll use it every day in Tokyo.

15
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:56,152
[Vocab] 走らせる

16
00:01:56,552 --> 00:02:06,176
[Host] To make something run. The base verb means to run. This form means to make something run. Trains run, but people make trains run.

17
00:02:06,775 --> 00:02:09,656
[Vocab] 考えています

18
00:02:10,056 --> 00:02:16,848
[Host] Is thinking about, is considering. It means they are currently thinking about it. No decision yet.

19
00:02:17,448 --> 00:02:19,032
[Host] Next sentence.

20
00:02:19,632 --> 00:02:26,352
[Slow] 今、東京の電車は夜12時ごろに止まります。

21
00:02:27,151 --> 00:02:30,608
[Host] Right now, Tokyo's trains stop around midnight.

22
00:02:31,207 --> 00:02:33,127
[Vocab] ごろ

23
00:02:33,527 --> 00:02:40,151
[Host] Around, approximately. But only for time. For amounts, you use a different word.

24
00:02:40,752 --> 00:02:43,199
[Vocab] 止まります

25
00:02:43,599 --> 00:02:48,448
[Host] Stops. One of the most useful verbs for daily life in Japan.

26
00:02:49,048 --> 00:02:50,919
[Host] Who needs this change?

27
00:02:51,520 --> 00:03:00,807
[Slow] 夜遅くまで働く人や、外国からの旅行者にとって、これは不便です。

28
00:03:01,608 --> 00:03:07,247
[Host] For people who work late at night and travelers from abroad, this is inconvenient.

29
00:03:07,848 --> 00:03:10,295
[Vocab] 働く

30
00:03:10,695 --> 00:03:15,975
[Host] To work. A very common verb. You'll hear it in many news stories.

31
00:03:16,575 --> 00:03:19,048
[Vocab] 旅行者

32
00:03:19,448 --> 00:03:24,967
[Host] Traveler. The first part means travel, the last character means person.

33
00:03:25,568 --> 00:03:27,632
[Vocab] 不便

34
00:03:28,032 --> 00:03:35,063
[Host] Inconvenient. The first character is a prefix that means not. The opposite means convenient.

35
00:03:35,663 --> 00:03:36,840
[Host] The plan.

36
00:03:37,439 --> 00:03:45,240
[Slow] まず、金曜日と土曜日の夜だけ、試してみる予定です。

37
00:03:46,039 --> 00:03:50,840
[Host] First, they plan to try it only on Friday and Saturday nights.

38
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:53,479
[Vocab] まず

39
00:03:53,879 --> 00:03:58,463
[Host] First, to begin with. A great word for explaining steps.

40
00:03:59,063 --> 00:04:01,704
[Vocab] 試してみる

41
00:04:02,104 --> 00:04:08,343
[Host] To try doing something. When you add this ending to a verb, it means let's try it and see.

42
00:04:08,943 --> 00:04:11,127
[Vocab] 予定

43
00:04:11,527 --> 00:04:16,016
[Host] Plan, schedule. Very useful for everyday conversation.

44
00:04:16,615 --> 00:04:18,560
[Host] Which lines will they use?

45
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:25,375
[Slow] 使う路線は、山手線と中央線です。

46
00:04:26,175 --> 00:04:35,247
[Host] The lines they'll use are the Yamanote Line and the Chuo Line. If you've been to Tokyo, you know these. The green circle line and the orange line.

47
00:04:35,848 --> 00:04:37,983
[Vocab] 路線

48
00:04:38,384 --> 00:04:42,848
[Host] Train line, route. Very common in news about transportation.

49
00:04:43,447 --> 00:04:45,175
[Host] But there's a problem.

50
00:04:45,776 --> 00:04:54,992
[Slow] でも、夜の間に線路の点検をしているので、安全の問題があります。

51
00:04:55,791 --> 00:05:00,255
[Host] But they do track inspections during the night, so there are safety concerns.

52
00:05:00,855 --> 00:05:03,016
[Vocab] 安全

53
00:05:03,415 --> 00:05:07,735
[Host] Safety. You'll see this word on signs everywhere in Japan.

54
00:05:08,336 --> 00:05:10,591
[Vocab] 問題

55
00:05:10,992 --> 00:05:14,855
[Host] Problem, issue. Another word you'll hear constantly.

56
00:05:15,456 --> 00:05:17,543
[Host] And the official's comment.

57
00:05:18,144 --> 00:05:26,016
[Slow] 安全が一番大切です。よく調べてから決めます。

58
00:05:26,815 --> 00:05:32,791
[Host] Safety is the most important thing. We will investigate carefully before deciding.

59
00:05:33,391 --> 00:05:35,672
[Vocab] 一番

60
00:05:36,072 --> 00:05:45,264
[Host] Number one, the most. You can combine it with any adjective. The most important. The most fun. Very useful pattern.

61
00:05:45,863 --> 00:05:48,312
[Vocab] 大切

62
00:05:48,711 --> 00:05:54,759
[Host] Important, precious. A warm word. You use it for things you truly care about.

63
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:57,735
[Vocab] 決めます

64
00:05:58,136 --> 00:06:02,288
[Host] To decide. A word you'll use a lot in daily life.

65
00:06:02,887 --> 00:06:05,887
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

66
00:06:06,487 --> 00:06:14,048
[News] 東京都は、電車を24時間走らせることを考えています。

67
00:06:14,747 --> 00:06:24,971
[News] 今、東京の電車は夜12時ごろに止まります。朝5時まで電車はありません。

68
00:06:25,672 --> 00:06:34,336
[News] 夜遅くまで働く人や、外国からの旅行者にとって、これは不便です。

69
00:06:35,036 --> 00:06:42,307
[News] まず、金曜日と土曜日の夜だけ、試してみる予定です。

70
00:06:43,007 --> 00:06:48,791
[News] 使う路線は、山手線と中央線です。

71
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:58,084
[News] でも、夜の間に線路の点検をしているので、安全の問題があります。

72
00:06:58,783 --> 00:07:10,016
[News] 東京都の担当者は、「安全が一番大切です。よく調べてから決めます」と言いました。

73
00:07:10,716 --> 00:07:13,451
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

74
00:07:14,052 --> 00:07:19,980
[Slow] 今、東京の電車は何時に止まりますか？

75
00:07:20,779 --> 00:07:24,572
[Host] What time do Tokyo trains stop? Around midnight.

76
00:07:25,172 --> 00:07:29,803
[Slow] まず、何曜日に試しますか？

77
00:07:30,603 --> 00:07:34,588
[Host] What days will they try first? Friday and Saturday.

78
00:07:35,187 --> 00:07:39,220
[Slow] 何が一番大切ですか？

79
00:07:40,019 --> 00:07:43,259
[Host] What is the most important thing? Safety.

80
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:56,244
[Host] That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

81
00:07:56,843 --> 00:07:59,244
[News] また明日。
